-- Door-in-wall fix (a post-roadmap addition, not one of the numbered
-- prompts) — no schema changes needed (asset_library already has everything
-- a preset row needs), just one new built-in preset row for the new wall
-- variant generated by scripts/assets/generate-wall-variants-presets.mjs:
--   - "Wall Doorway" (wall-door.glb): a wall segment with an actual walkable
--     doorway cut into its own mass — templates.ts's walledRoom/
--     buildingOutline/multiDoorRoom now place this INSTEAD of a plain "Wall
--     Segment" at a door cell, replacing the old approach of placing the
--     free-standing "Door" preset (a55e7003) at ground level next to intact
--     wall cells one full elevation step above it. "Door" (a55e7003) stays
--     seeded/unchanged — still a legitimate free-standing/interior door, just
--     no longer what any built-in template places at a wall-perimeter door
--     cell — see PRESET_WALL_DOOR's own doc comment in templates.ts.
--
-- This migration also picks up wall-corner.glb/wall-diagonal.glb's own
-- REGENERATED geometry (same task, same script run) — a real, measured
-- height/footprint mismatch between the straight Wall Segment and the
-- existing Wall Corner/Wall Diagonal pieces (see
-- generate-wall-variants-presets.mjs's own top comment for the exact
-- numbers). Those two rows already exist from 0055_wall_variants.sql and
-- point at the SAME file paths, so no new row is needed for them here — only
-- the two .glb files on disk changed, which this migration doesn't touch.
--
-- Seeded via migration as postgres, bypassing RLS, the identical
-- 0016_asset_library_presets.sql / 0053_crossing_structures.sql /
-- 0055_wall_variants.sql reasoning: 0015's insert policy forbids preset rows
-- (campaign_id null) through the app path, so presets are seeded data by
-- design. Fixed UUID one past 0055's last (…011, Wall Diagonal) — keeps
-- every built-in preset's identity in one inspectable a55e7NNN numbering
-- scheme across environments.
--
-- `on conflict do nothing` guards re-application the same way every prior
-- preset-seeding migration does, in case a dev stack already has this row
-- from a direct, non-migration-tracked application under a different
-- filename (other concurrent agents may apply migrations directly to the
-- shared dev DB during testing).
insert into public.asset_library (id, name, source_type, model_ref) values
  ('a55e7012-0000-4000-8000-000000000012', 'Wall Doorway', 'preset', '/assets/presets/wall-door.glb')
on conflict (id) do nothing;
